WEBVTT

00:08.340 --> 00:15.540
Omoi wo ima hanadete hatenai asu ni kazasu yo

00:08.340 --> 00:15.540
I now play my feelings,
out to the endless tomorrow!

00:15.580 --> 00:22.290
Setsunai hodo mune utsu kagirinai kibou

00:15.580 --> 00:22.290
This unbounded hope that beats in my breast
to the point of melancholy

00:23.090 --> 00:30.890
Hakanasa wo masu hibi wo
irodoru wa kisetsu no kaze

00:23.090 --> 00:30.890
The days pass by, becoming more fleeting,
colored by the season's wind

00:30.930 --> 00:35.600
Kioku no kakera ga sawagidashita yo

00:30.930 --> 00:35.600
The fragments of memory started running wild

00:36.200 --> 00:44.600
Arinomama wo mitomete
haruka tsumuida hikari ga

00:36.200 --> 00:44.600
One more time, I want to hold the
spindle of far off light close to my breast,

00:44.650 --> 00:52.280
Kieru mae ni mou ichido
kono mune ni dakishimete

00:44.650 --> 00:52.280
Before it disappears, before
I accept the way things are now

00:54.360 --> 01:01.560
Omoi wo ima hanadete hatenai asu ni kazasu yo

00:54.360 --> 01:01.560
I now play my feelings,
out to the endless tomorrow!

01:01.560 --> 01:08.700
Mirai wo egaku ao ni kono te wo nobashite

01:01.560 --> 01:08.700
Hold out this hand to the blue-painted future

01:08.870 --> 01:16.000
Kasokushiteku sekai yo douka
yasashii mama de ite

01:08.870 --> 01:16.000
The world accelerates, please let it stay this kind

01:16.110 --> 01:23.610
Setsunai hodo mune utsu afuredasu negai

01:16.110 --> 01:23.610
This overflowing wish that beats in my breast
to the point of melancholy

01:47.970 --> 01:50.100
Manatsu?

01:58.210 --> 01:59.840
The bubbles are...

02:05.850 --> 02:07.120
That's...

02:09.860 --> 02:11.020
...me?

02:17.370 --> 02:18.800
Manatsu!

02:25.210 --> 02:27.140
That was the dream.

02:28.580 --> 02:30.510
Without any reason for it,

02:30.510 --> 02:37.250
I believed it was a dream created
by my heart and Manatsu's feelings.

02:39.220 --> 02:44.560
But I didn't think it could actually be reality.

02:45.560 --> 02:50.060
The Surge of Separation

02:59.840 --> 03:02.870
Sei, stay there, asleep.

03:03.610 --> 03:08.450
It's best for you not to see
what happens from now on.

03:10.650 --> 03:12.350
You are kind.

03:16.290 --> 03:18.560
Finally here!

03:20.500 --> 03:23.560


03:23.570 --> 03:24.600
I'm back!

03:24.600 --> 03:26.870
I am so not a morning person!

03:26.870 --> 03:28.060
Welcome back.

03:29.440 --> 03:33.910
I'm gonna go back to sleep until breakfast.

03:33.910 --> 03:34.930
Ichika dear.

03:36.340 --> 03:40.180
Ichika dear, will you start to pack up
little by little?

03:40.180 --> 03:42.310
Yes, I will.

03:43.190 --> 03:46.210
There's only a week until we move, you know.

03:47.890 --> 03:50.120
A week...

03:58.730 --> 04:01.970
Another week before you
move to Milan, Tachibana...

04:02.300 --> 04:07.470
Even Italy's Tornatore recognizes
your talents, Tachibana.

04:08.380 --> 04:11.570
It's just a meeting of minds for the joint venture.

04:11.880 --> 04:14.420
The basic frame is going along well,

04:14.420 --> 04:17.410
and it seems like they're waiting for you
to come in person, Tachibana.

04:17.890 --> 04:21.960
The next five years are going to be hard
on your wife and daughter.

04:21.960 --> 04:23.120
Yeah...

04:23.130 --> 04:25.890
But as long as the foundation is sound,

04:25.890 --> 04:28.500
a few things here and there won't matter.

04:28.500 --> 04:30.300
Same goes for buildings, and people.

04:43.950 --> 04:44.740
Are you okay?

04:45.410 --> 04:47.400
Don't push yourself.

04:53.220 --> 04:55.220
Thank you.

04:55.220 --> 04:57.620
Huh, food?

04:57.960 --> 05:00.760
There was a time she could not eat...

05:01.460 --> 05:04.260
But like that child from the past...

05:07.140 --> 05:08.630
What is amusing?

05:10.470 --> 05:13.880
You should know better than anyone.

05:13.880 --> 05:16.940
Every human is different.

05:17.380 --> 05:21.580
So am I. And so is her.

05:24.120 --> 05:25.850
That's enough, Ichika.

05:25.850 --> 05:28.560
I just need to put them in the dish washer.

05:28.560 --> 05:29.390
Right...

05:36.930 --> 05:39.660
What happened after that?

05:40.670 --> 05:44.310
Ichika, I'm going to tell you the truth.

05:44.310 --> 05:45.540
I...

05:48.940 --> 05:50.810
Sei?

05:53.950 --> 05:57.120
Sei isn't answering his phone or mails...

05:57.120 --> 06:02.280


06:02.690 --> 06:06.320
At this rate I might not be able to say goodbye...

06:08.060 --> 06:09.830
Yes? This is Ichika!

06:10.370 --> 06:12.530
Hello, hello, Ichika!

06:12.530 --> 06:15.230
We're heading to the pool, wanna come?

06:15.600 --> 06:18.170
I'm here with Keiko.

06:18.170 --> 06:20.110
Hiya, Ichika!

06:20.110 --> 06:22.010
Michiru said she's coming, too.

06:22.010 --> 06:24.080
The pool?

06:24.080 --> 06:25.640
You have some other plans?

06:26.350 --> 06:28.440
There's only a week...

06:29.890 --> 06:32.220
I only have a week...

06:32.650 --> 06:34.790
No, I don't.

06:34.790 --> 06:36.920
Then I'll be waiting with Keiko.

06:36.930 --> 06:38.720
Bring Manatsu along!

06:39.830 --> 06:40.590
Sure.

06:58.310 --> 06:59.440
You're loud.

07:00.750 --> 07:03.820
But, it's trying so hard...

07:03.820 --> 07:08.320
After spending so long in the soil,
it's only able to live above ground...

07:08.820 --> 07:10.950
...for about a week...

07:13.030 --> 07:14.660
Ichika!

07:15.800 --> 07:16.730
Michiru!

07:20.900 --> 07:23.960
Ooh, it's a hotel pool!

07:34.750 --> 07:38.080
What, you came wearing it
under your clothes again?

07:39.290 --> 07:41.260
So did you, Satsuki!

07:41.990 --> 07:43.650
Hey!

07:45.490 --> 07:47.190
What's the matter, Ichika?

07:47.700 --> 07:50.260
You've seemed down lately.

07:51.270 --> 07:53.290
That's not true...

07:56.640 --> 08:00.780
But wait... This place is expensive, right?

08:00.780 --> 08:03.300
Wouldn't a public pool be better?

08:04.310 --> 08:06.340
Are you serious?

08:07.620 --> 08:09.950
That's the public pool.

08:09.950 --> 08:11.280
Next door?

08:12.820 --> 08:16.050
Keiko had some free passes.

08:16.360 --> 08:18.830
Thank you very much, Keiko.

08:18.830 --> 08:20.300
Are you sure?

08:20.300 --> 08:22.530
Sure, no problem.

08:22.530 --> 08:24.060
Wow!

08:24.070 --> 08:25.530
Guess we're just lucky.

08:25.830 --> 08:27.940
Roger!

08:27.940 --> 08:31.540
I kind of feel like "why aren't we just
swimming in the ocean" though.

08:31.540 --> 08:33.510
Don't say that!

08:40.220 --> 08:43.420
So she's not afraid of water?

08:43.420 --> 08:46.440
She just can't handle saltwater, remember?

08:48.320 --> 08:51.050
But this is a pool, so it's no problem, right?

08:51.530 --> 08:52.320
Yes.

08:52.690 --> 08:56.960
But Michiru, you have the "vision"...

08:56.970 --> 09:02.230
Can you see dead sailors
or sea monsters in the ocean?

09:04.410 --> 09:06.430
Wait, seriously?

09:11.550 --> 09:13.540
Is that for real, Michiru?

09:14.750 --> 09:16.240
I wonder.

09:18.250 --> 09:22.750
I wondered how Michiru saw Manatsu.

09:23.560 --> 09:29.160
But I was scared to hear the answer
even if I asked.

09:34.000 --> 09:36.530
It's already been six years...

09:59.360 --> 10:03.500
You... You're...

10:03.500 --> 10:04.800
I'm Kai!

10:23.950 --> 10:28.450
In the end, will Ichika be faced
with the same fate?

10:29.160 --> 10:31.850
The fate of one chosen as a child of the trials...

10:33.560 --> 10:34.490
Sei...

10:56.080 --> 10:58.090
Satsuki...

10:58.090 --> 10:59.990
Take that!

11:01.960 --> 11:03.450
Sorry, my bad!

11:04.230 --> 11:05.730
Take that!

11:05.730 --> 11:07.130
That dream...

11:12.630 --> 11:14.730
I wonder what it means?

11:18.740 --> 11:20.370
What is wrong?

11:20.880 --> 11:24.110
We're wondering if something's up with Ichika.

11:32.120 --> 11:35.850
Everyone has things they are worried about.

11:36.360 --> 11:37.380
Everyone.

11:38.330 --> 11:39.350
Yeah...

11:41.900 --> 11:43.760
What are you guys doing?

11:44.500 --> 11:46.060
Manatsu!

11:50.100 --> 11:52.940
You are Ichika, yes?

11:54.010 --> 12:01.470
When summer break started,
and Manatsu came, you changed a little.

12:02.320 --> 12:08.280
But you are still the Ichika that we know, yes?

12:08.920 --> 12:09.820
Oh, no!

12:09.820 --> 12:11.390
My heart beating like this...

12:11.390 --> 12:13.660
What are you saying?

12:14.900 --> 12:19.730
Because, Manatsu... She is...

12:26.980 --> 12:29.310
Manatsu, flawless victory!

12:29.310 --> 12:31.140
Yay!

12:32.410 --> 12:35.720
The seven ordeals imposed
on the children of the trials...

12:35.720 --> 12:38.120
And the seven great vices.

12:38.720 --> 12:42.950
Losing their pure innocence,
cornered into a decision.

12:56.270 --> 12:58.640
Saya?

12:58.640 --> 13:03.240
Now, let me hear your decision, Sei.

13:04.480 --> 13:06.750
I... I...

13:06.750 --> 13:07.580
Sei!

13:07.850 --> 13:09.580
I can't!

13:09.580 --> 13:12.990
I can't... choose...

13:13.820 --> 13:18.320
Choosing neither...
That is not one of the choices.

13:19.090 --> 13:21.060
That's a violation of the rules.

13:21.360 --> 13:22.960
A violation of the rules?

13:23.300 --> 13:27.240
What does that mean?

13:27.240 --> 13:28.500
Saya!

13:30.740 --> 13:34.040
It seems this trial was a failure.

13:37.150 --> 13:38.610
Too bad...

13:39.350 --> 13:40.370
Sei!

13:40.880 --> 13:42.540
What are you doing?

13:45.420 --> 13:46.510
I...

13:47.660 --> 13:50.390
All I did was cause you suffering.

13:51.530 --> 13:52.620
This whole time...

13:53.490 --> 13:54.520
Sei...

14:07.310 --> 14:08.710
What is wrong?

14:10.580 --> 14:12.880
I'm just a little tired.

14:13.250 --> 14:14.110
In that case...

14:22.160 --> 14:25.790
Ichika, are you worried about something?

14:26.760 --> 14:32.700
We might not be so close as to not
keep secrets from one another.

14:33.070 --> 14:36.660
But we are not such strangers to not open up
when something is worrying us, yes?

14:37.410 --> 14:40.570
I'm not worried about anything.

14:40.910 --> 14:42.340
Is that so?

14:46.150 --> 14:49.780
Michiru, you see...

14:50.080 --> 14:51.950
Don't you worry 'bout that!

14:51.950 --> 14:54.560
I'll take responsibility, I promise.

14:54.560 --> 14:57.020
Here, let's pinky swear!

14:57.020 --> 14:59.790
Don't tell anyone, promise?

15:01.360 --> 15:04.420
Ichika, that's breaking the rules...

15:05.830 --> 15:06.990
I...

15:08.000 --> 15:10.400
But... But I'm...

15:11.610 --> 15:13.010
I'm transferring schools!

15:17.880 --> 15:22.040
I might be moving.

15:24.420 --> 15:25.350
We know.

15:26.920 --> 15:30.690
Before the first term ending ceremony,
Ms. Hinata...

15:31.660 --> 15:36.160
I didn't want everyone to know I was moving.

15:36.500 --> 15:38.930
I didn't want it to weigh on everyone.

15:39.430 --> 15:43.930
I wanted to spend my final summer
like I always did.

15:44.240 --> 15:45.100
And yet...

15:45.410 --> 15:47.070
It'll be for five years, I hear.

15:47.740 --> 15:51.910
Tachibana will probably not be
coming back to this academy.

15:52.310 --> 15:53.210
So...

15:54.450 --> 15:56.750
Everyone knew?

15:58.190 --> 16:02.690
But that isn't the only thing
that is worrying you, right?

16:03.520 --> 16:06.050
The huge power outage at Enoshima...

16:10.970 --> 16:12.600
Has Manatsu...

16:12.600 --> 16:16.470
Has she got you wrapped up
in something dangerous, Ichika?

16:22.780 --> 16:27.040
It doesn't have anything to do with you all.

16:28.450 --> 16:29.540
Ichika...

16:36.920 --> 16:39.020
Huh? The tide...

16:40.260 --> 16:43.360
A Djinn... The eleventh Djinn is...

16:45.330 --> 16:46.860
Ichika?

16:47.840 --> 16:48.860
Ichika!

17:00.410 --> 17:02.540
Ichi...ka...

17:19.500 --> 17:21.400
The spirit of the sea...

17:21.970 --> 17:23.370
The Djinn, Oceana.

17:27.610 --> 17:30.840
Ichika... Snap out of it, Ichika!

17:37.720 --> 17:39.020
A tsunami!

17:41.060 --> 17:44.360
I've never seen one that big...

17:47.860 --> 17:49.420
You're not going to run?

17:51.200 --> 17:54.330
There's no time, is there?

18:03.740 --> 18:05.250
This is my fault...

18:05.250 --> 18:09.080
If I can get the Djinn to listen to my heart again...

18:09.080 --> 18:10.450
It's no use, Ichika!

18:10.450 --> 18:13.320
You can't stop that wave
no matter what you do!

18:18.890 --> 18:21.300
Stop! Please stop!

18:21.300 --> 18:23.020
Stop the wave!

18:23.430 --> 18:25.770
I'm begging you, stop it!

18:25.770 --> 18:27.170
Please!

18:29.400 --> 18:32.810
Ichika!

18:41.180 --> 18:43.210
That's a violation of the rules.

19:28.360 --> 19:29.800
Foolish child.

19:31.700 --> 19:32.930
Wait...

19:41.640 --> 19:45.080
But now there is one left.

19:46.380 --> 19:49.850
Ichika, Manatsu!

19:49.850 --> 19:52.790
Ichika, Manatsu!

19:56.460 --> 19:57.950
Manatsu...

19:59.590 --> 20:03.760
Manatsu saved me... And...

20:03.760 --> 20:04.970
Ichika...

20:04.970 --> 20:06.260
Manatsu!

20:07.570 --> 20:10.230
Are you sure you're okay by yourself, Ichika?

20:10.840 --> 20:12.270
Should I call a car?

20:12.670 --> 20:13.940
We're okay.

20:15.910 --> 20:17.210
Michiru...

20:31.760 --> 20:33.820
Saya?

20:35.100 --> 20:38.870
Ichika, do you know that woman?

20:38.870 --> 20:41.130
What do you mean?

20:41.140 --> 20:44.800
I sense the same feeling from her
as I do from Manatsu.

20:46.510 --> 20:48.680
But that's...

20:48.680 --> 20:51.010
But lately...

20:52.480 --> 20:56.280
Lately you seem more and more
like them too, Ichika.

21:28.720 --> 21:30.010
Ichika?

21:30.550 --> 21:31.920
Ichika?

21:31.920 --> 21:33.350
Ichika!

21:47.470 --> 21:50.440


21:51.210 --> 22:00.770
Ano hi deawanakereba ima mo
waraeteta no ka na?

21:51.210 --> 22:00.770
If we hadn't met that day,
would I have still been able to laugh now?

22:02.150 --> 22:13.650
Ano hi nakushita egao itsuka tokeru namida

22:02.150 --> 22:13.650
The smile I lost that day,
the tears that one day melt away...

22:19.170 --> 22:28.940
Hora kotoshi mo ame furu gogo
hakanai utakata no iro

22:19.170 --> 22:28.940
See, this year the afternoon rain falls again
in the color of fleeting bubbles

22:30.010 --> 22:38.850
Sora mo yasashiku mienai wa
datte hitori da mono

22:30.010 --> 22:38.850
The sky doesn't look kind to me, after all,
I'm alone

22:40.490 --> 22:45.490
Itazura na sadame ni kotoba mo denai wa

22:40.490 --> 22:45.490
I have no more words for the tricks of fate

22:45.890 --> 22:53.290
Wakariaeta futari ni mou modorenai no?

22:45.890 --> 22:53.290
Can we never return to two
who understood each other?

22:53.870 --> 23:03.470
Ano hi deawanakereba ima mo
waraeteta no ka na?

22:53.870 --> 23:03.470
If we hadn't met that day,
would I have still been able to laugh now?

23:04.850 --> 23:16.550
Ano hi nakushita egao itsuka tokeru namida

23:04.850 --> 23:16.550
The smile I lost that day,
the tears that one day melt away...

23:21.800 --> 23:24.530
Even if I have to exchange my life for it.

23:25.030 --> 23:27.300
Even if I have to exchange the world for it.

23:28.070 --> 23:34.410
On that day I came to realize that it truly existed.

23:35.210 --> 23:40.210
On the next Uta~Kata:
The Poetry of Fragments
